<h1 class="pageh1">FAQ</h1>
	<br>
	<br>

<div style="text-indent: 28px; font-size: 16px; text-align:left; padding-left: 10px;padding-right: 10px;" >

<!--Accounts-->

<h3 class="pageh3">General</h3>
		<div class="q1">
		<p class="question">Q: Why do I need to register to use the basic or free tax calculator? </p>
		<p class="answer">A: We do not endorse or condone bots or the misuse of our services. In order to facilitate this, we require all users to register for a free account as this provides us with the metrics to stop abuse.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="q2">
		<p class="question">Q: Can I share my account or let a friend log in with my credentials?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: No.
			<br><br>  It is a violation of our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy to share accounts or use an account for bots or other illicit activity.  This is considered an abuse of our services and will be handled accordingly.  
			<br><br>  If an account is found to be in violation of our policies we will terminate the account immediately.
			<br><br>  If you feel this has occurred in error, you can appeal your case via the feedback form, email, or with us on our Discord.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="q1">
			<p class="question">Q: I just signed up.  How do I subscribe?</p>
			<p class="answer">A: After signing up, you will receive an e-mail containing a link to verify the account.<br>
				<br>Once the e-mail provided is verified, you will then be able to subscribe.<br>
				<br>You can subscribe for our services in multiple places, including your User Profile, the About Page, or the Tax Tool itself.
				<br>
				<br>
				If you did not receive a verification e-mail, please reach out to us at <a href="mailto:Accounts@Taxov.Tax" style="color: #9a8866">Accounts@Taxov.Tax</a>.
			</p>


		</div>

<h3 class="pageh3">Accounts / Billing</h3>

		<div class="q1">
		<p class="question">Q: Who can I contact in regards to my Taxov account? (Accounts / Billing / Services)</p>
		<p class="answer">A: Generally, contacting us on Discord will be the fastest method.  However, you can also reach us by e-mail at <a href="mailto:Accounts@Taxov.Tax" style="color: #9a8866">Accounts@Taxov.Tax</a> or <a href="mailto:Billing@Taxov.Tax" style="color: #9a8866">Billing@Taxov.Tax</a>.
			<br><br>

			Navigate to the Contact Page via the Main Menu for other contact information. </p>
		</div>	
		
		<div class="q2">
		<p class="question">Q: How is my subscription billed?  Can I pay one month at a time?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: After successful subscription and payment processing, your billing cycle will begin.
			<br><br>  Your subscription is billed at recurring monthly intervals.  You can check the date and time your subscription will expire/renew on your User Profile Page.
			<br><br>  If you prefer to pay on a month to month basis, you can do so by subscribing as normal, and then canceling your subscription before the billing cycle ends.
			<br><br>  You can manage your subscription information on your User Profile Page.
			<br><br>  When canceling your subscription you will retain access to your current service until the subscription period has expired.  </p>
		</div>

		<div class="q1">
		<p class="question">Q: I just subscribed but now wish to upgrade my plan.  Will I be charged twice?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: When upgrading, you will pay for your new plan as normal.
			<br><br>  After a successful upgrade transaction, you will then be refunded the pro-rated amount for the remaining time on your previous subscription plan.
			
			<br><br>  Your new billing cycle will start upon successful payment for your new upgraded plan.
			
			</p>
			
			@*<p class="question">Example:</p>
			<p class="answer" style="font-style:italic">You are currently subscribed to the Semi-Auto and wish to upgrade to the Full Auto plan.</p>
			<p class="answer" style="font-style:italic">  You have used only 10 days of your original plan before choosing to upgrade.</p>
			<p class="answer" style="font-style:italic">  Upon upgrading you will be charged the new subscription rate - ($5/mo)</p>
			<p class="answer" style="font-style:italic">  You will then be refunded for the remaining time on your original plan.</p>
			<p class="answer" style="font-style:italic">  (20 days remaining = $2 pro-rated refund)</p>*@
		</div>	
		
		<div class="q2">
		<p class="question">Q: What if I have accidentally canceled my subscription?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: Navigate to your User Profile Page and click the "Reactivate Subscription" button.  Your subscription will then return to automatic billing.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="q1">
		<p class="question">Q: What happens if there is an error or glitch during the subscription process?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: If the error occurs with the payment processor (Stripe), the transaction will cancel before any charges are made.
			<br><br>  If the error occurs between payment processing and syncing to the Taxov servers, the transaction will be canceled and you will 
			be issued a refund in full.
			<br><br>  If the error persists, please contact <a href="mailto:Billing@Taxov.Tax" style="color: #9a8866">Billing@Taxov.Tax</a> for assistance.</p>
		</div>	

		<div class="q2">
		<p class="question">Q: I just subscribed but I do not have access, what do I do?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: Please allow a few moments for our servers to update before refreshing the page.
			<br><br>  You may also force an update from your User Profile Page by clicking the "Refresh" button.
			<br><br>  If this does not resolve the issue, do not hesitate to contact us.  You 
			may do so via our Discord or through our Contact Page at the top of the Navigation Bar.
			<br><br>  Please have the relative information readily available so we may assist you with your issue.</p>
		</div>	

<h3 class="pageh3">Tax Calculator</h3>
		<div class="q1">
		<p class="question">Q: I think the calculator may have a bug/glitch.  How can I report this?</p>
		<p class="answer">A: In the event of a bug that will not resolve itself with a simple page refresh, please provide detailed feedback to us on our Discord Feedback Form.</p>
		</div>
			
</div>
